-- title:
--   RSP initialization, tournament and edge-expectation correctness
-- statement:
--   The structured register-machine commands implement finite loops, tournament repair and construction, shortest-tree initialization and relaxation, geometric-guess setup, sparse output records, and the Poisson edge-expectation calculation. They preserve their specified register and memory representations and obey the stated instruction bounds. The accompanying path, queue and probability identities provide the invariants used by these implementations.
--
--   Writing $P_1,\ldots,P_{842}$ for the fully quantified component properties, with their respective hypotheses, the assertion is
--
--   $$\bigwedge_{r=1}^{842}P_r.$$
--
--   These properties supply the implementation interface used by table construction, deterministic retrieval and the outer approximation guarantee.
-- source:
--   A Deterministic Near-Linear Time Approximation Algorithm for Restricted Shortest Paths in Directed Graphs, Theorem 1 (p. 3), Section 4 (pp. 6–8), and Observation A.1 (p. 14). Derived initialization, implementation and expectation lemmas for the two-resource formalization: https://prove2.me/missions/A_Deterministic_Near-Linear_Time_Approximation_Algorithm_for_Restricted_Shortest_Paths_in_Directed_Graphs

